    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think the biggest surprise would be, and I guess it's a bigger surprise than I thought. is the amount to how complicated and big Washington is. It's very difficult to navigate through, and it shouldn't be that way. When you have a big government, centralized government system like this, that was never meant to be so centralized, that people end up losing their ability to understand what's going on, to be able to make their voices heard in Washington. And it's been my mission to do everything I can to get the decision-making as close to people as possible. simplify Washington here, make Washington smaller so that people can be bigger.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
