    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90234.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "Well, I'm on financial services. It's pretty much doing everything I can to create an opportunity where people can get credit, where the finances are a little bit more liquid, so that it's not difficult for people to be able to get a loan for a small business if they need to be able to get the credit to get into a home. For a lot of people, that is just the basic of the American dream. So, you know, again, a lot of the banking regulation comes and is driven right out of Washington. And I tend to like the, tend to allow, like to allow people to really engage with their consumers, to get to the basic needs of their consumers so that everyone can get that individual type of a type of relationship with whatever financial institution that they get. Utah has a big presence in financial services, so that was also a big reason why this committee was a good fit for me. This is again, and keeping the promises that I made to people, doing everything I can so that they can get goods and services at the lowest price",
