  {
    "episode_id": 90234,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90234.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 19,
    "turn_text": "while you're here? Gosh, you know, I guess it boils down to one thing, all of the decisions I make, if Washington's less powerful, If people have the ability, have their freedoms back and have the ability to be the authors of their life, then I would have accomplished what I set to do. Hopefully I'm not here too long. I want to still be young and enjoy my family. But we're all my family and I, we're all in this together. This is all of our journey and it's part of Utah's journey also. And so, you know, while we're doing this, I hope that my children can learn from this process. I hope that I can bring Utah along with me through this process and Utah becomes a little bit bigger, more recognized for the things that we're doing. I hope that at the end of the day that that's what happens that we end up getting the decision-making schools to people again.",
