  {
    "episode_id": 90234,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90234.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "I think one of the comments that I get was, how did you get elected in the state of Utah? And I think that they're referring to the fact that I'm the only female in the delegation that I am a mother with three kids. I am a black American. But I guess the people start taking notice because Utah's more concerned about getting things done. Utah's more concerned and more family oriented. And so, you know, I think that there's this idea of Utah. that is starting to change and how we are growing very quickly. We've got very young families. We are more than up and coming. We're actually solving problems even in areas like intergenerational poverty. We are doing really well in our low employment rates. So Utah is on the map for many, many reasons. And most of the time I just tell people to just follow the sun and you'll find Utah. But I think that's the reason why we're on the map. It's because we're less concerned about what people look like. We're more concerned about getting things done. We're more concerned about solving problems and doing what's best for the next 40 to 50 years as opposed to doing what's best for the next",
