    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90234.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 28,
    "turn_text": "Well, it's actually the select committee to investigate infants and what's happening in that area. And I have to say that it's important that we tread very carefully. There's a lot that we don't know about what's happening in this industry in terms of the procurement of and the sales of body parts. I think first and foremost, it's my job to protect human life. But even with that being said, there's so many questions out there that it's also my job to go on a fact-finding mission and to be as transparent as possible and let the American people decide what they want to do with the information that they get. And so, yeah, it's not going to be an easy committee. I'm honored as a freshman that I was chosen to be on this committee. I don't think there has been a freshman ever selected to be on a special select committee like this. I really appreciate and certainly I'm honored to have been chosen for this committee, but there's a lot of responsibility, making sure that I'm fair, that I just go on a fact-finding mission and let the American people decide what they want to do with the information that is given to them.",
