    "turn_text": "Well, let's start off by what we've seen in the results. Paul Ryan got 95%. One of the highest percentages that any speaker has gotten in the majority. So that's an indicator itself. I voted for Paul Ryan and Mitt Romney for the presidency, the vice president and president of the United States. I think that especially the way that Paul Ryan wants to structure the restructure, the seat, the speaker seat, I think it's exactly the type of shift we need. And what I mean by that is we, in the majority, have been behaving as if we're in the minority. And the position of the minority is to just oppose. And we can't, and we're even bad at that, by the way. We're terrible at even opposing. It's what I've been saying for a long time. We've got to go out and talk to people about what we're for. Why conservative policies have actually taking more people out of poverty than any other policy. I've seen them work as a mayor. I've seen them work as a mother. With conservative policies, no one in this country is predestined to be poor. I think it's important for us to go out and talk about how this is going to help, not just one particular American, but all Americans across the board, that people can be as ordinary or as extraordinary as they choose to be. One last thing I wanted to mention is I had a town hall meeting where I invited veterans to come out and speak to us. And one lady came who was not a vet and this black woman came and said, you know, I wanted to come and hear you speak because I've been a liberal all my life. And she said, I woke up one day and I realized that liberals give you exactly what you need to stay exactly where you are. And your policies, the things that you've talked about, are saying that I have the opportunity to actually go a little bit further and have not just what I need, but some of the things that I want. And I can be as ordinary or as extraordinary as I choose to be. And so I think that that message is resonating. I have hope for this country or else I wouldn't be here. I have hope that we're moving in the right direction, this conference. New leadership is good. Nice, fresh, young, really ambitious and active. Leaders are what's needed to invigorate this country. I still believe that we live in the best country on Earth. And it's my job, my responsibility as an American, as a mom, as a Utahn to continue to fight for this country.",
